 05 
 158th/A  
 Dragons  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 223rd Phalanx, the 75th Dragons and the 106th 
Dragons in reserve.  Standing at the ready with her warriors was Tlazolteotl.
No generals were present to lead the forces of Prometeo.
  Tlazolteotl seemed lucky, for she was able to convince a native tribe to 
fight for her cause.  But her luck turned sour when the provincial Eagle 
chieftain bribed Tlazolteotl's ally to switch sides, which gave the 
provincial Eagle chieftain a clear advantage.  On the other hand Tlazolteotl
's wise tactical planning assured her side a clear superiority.
  Prometeo soon found that the Dragons would rather swallow spears than obey 
a repulsive creature like Prometeo.
  Across the whole front, the Elite 139th Phalanx faced the 158th Dragons.  
The 256th Dragons soared over the 158th Dragons and attacked without mercy.  
The 222nd Phalanx outflanked the undermanned enemy and attacked with full 
strength.  The 139th Phalanx battled with the 158th Dragons and mowed them 
down like weeds.
  Having found a vulnerable spot in the line of the host of Prometeo, a 
final savage slashing attack defeated their opponent and won the day for 
Tlazolteotl.  The 256th Dragons gave chase and annihilated the 158th Dragons.
  Shasta was overrun by the forces of Tlazolteotl.  The provincial Eagle 
chieftain set out for Mongu with its motley army.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Plain province of Cantia, 
ruled by Prometeo.  Pascal (#78)'s forces encountered little opposition in 
Cantia and Pascal there established our reign.  Pascal leads approximately 1 
Legion and 1 Chariots.
  In early summer, Prometeo could not recruit Eagles in Shasta because 
Prometeo does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't available.  
Instead, Prometeo discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  In late summer, Prometeo travelled to Moongard.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into the fall.  Prometeo rode into the Io 
Sea.  To the east lies a poor Jungle area named Zululand (#506), populated 
by Humans.  It is ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  Their Human 
fighters array themselves as Legion and Fleet.  Southeast of here lies the 
prosperous province of the Crab Sea (#507), ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is known to be a Sea province 
inhabited by Whales.  If need be, they can muster a host of Whales to defend 
their territory.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, a man can see a Plain 
province known as Rosehaven (#407).  It is said that 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Humans.  Their Human fighters traditionally array themselves as Axemen.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Birchwood, a 
Forest area owned by Prometeo.  Teleko (#72)'s armies took possession of 
Birchwood practically uncontested.  Teleko leads approximately 1 Dragons, 4 
Eagles and 2 Trolls.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Marzuq, a Desert province owing its allegiance to 
Prometeo.  Pascal (#78)'s forces took Marzuq without any major engagements.  
Pascal leads approximately 1 Legion and 1 Chariots.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Prometeo moved into Big Sky.


  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
invaded the El Kalaa Sea, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by 
Prometeo and made up of great Jungles.  The El Kalaa Sea was overrun and 
occupied by Teleko (#72)'s host.  Teleko leads approximately 1 Dragons, 6 
Eagles and 2 Trolls.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Prometeo treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo 
treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Ashley (#74) got into trouble with a sheriff in Tesawa and escaped by 
riding away to Plumwood.


  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 15 gold in revenue.  8 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  6 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left 
with 55 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I failed in my ineffectual attempt to cast a Resurrection spell.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I travelled to Tesawa.
  In late summer, I journeyed to Mare Imbrium.
  With the coming of the fall season, I moved into Alderwood.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  In Alderwood, I commanded the 
232nd Legion, the 257th Legion and the 258th Legion to join forces with my 
army.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Ishtar discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early summer season Ishtar invented nothing worthy 
of note in his sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Ishtar was tutored in 
the art of Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar tried to practice his Sageness, but 
the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  His efforts improved his aptitude in 
Sageness.  He invented nothing worthy of note in his sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the fall season, Ishtar was tutored in the art of 
Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar rehearsed and practiced his Sageness and improved 
noticeably.
  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Sageness.  At levels 5 
and up, there is not necessarily an increase in the chance to invent 
something.  Instead, the Sage attracts a company of philosphers and builds a 
University in his province of birth.  Your characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  In his sagely researches, Ishtar discovered a fabulous invention called 
the Invisible Ink!  The following benefits are conferred by the Invisible 
Ink:
  Invisible Ink helps a spy to keep notes without the risk of being exposed 
as a spy.  Its effect is to raise the Spy ability of all of the characters 
of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  With the advent of the early winter season, Ishtar invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring, and I made ready to carry out my 
urgent assignments.  My attempted cast of the Oratory spell didn't work.
  During early summer, I marched my forces into Belladonna (#302).
  With the coming of the late summer season, I cancelled my move to Marzuq 
in order to fight for the province of Belladonna.  So, I practiced my 
Necromancy diligently for many weeks, but could make no progress.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) sent an invasion force into the 
adjacent Forest province of Belladonna, owned by Prometeo.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces were commanded by me.  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Belladonna (0302):

